BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eight Step Recovery Group For Men
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260514T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260514T183000
UID:64f5f11e526e0ac94f0f55ce@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Eight Step Recovery is an alternative recovery program to the 
 12-Step program of Alcoholic Anonymous. The program is a set of mindfulnes
 s teachings outlining a suggested course of action for recovery from addic
 tion\, stinking thinking\, negative mental states\, and compulsive and obs
 essive behaviours.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/eight-step-recovery-for-
 men-14-may
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kum Nye Tibetan Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260514T173000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260514T183000
UID:9561862d3bf26ce72953081a@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Kum Nye is a Tibetan movement practice\, similar to tai chi or
  yoga. This taster session explores simple exercises using movement\, brea
 th and awareness to release tension and develop a deeper sense of ease in 
 both body and mind. It loosely translates as 'attention to or massage of t
 he subtle body' and is suitable for all ages and most levels of fitness an
 d flexibility.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/kum-nye-tibetan-yoga-tas
 ter-14-may
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thursday Night Class: Meditation & In-Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260514T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260514T211500
UID:f6ecfc3fe1e75b1e79329153@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:These pith teachings - such as 'reduce input' and 'don't accep
 t yourself' - were given to members of our Buddhist Order by its founder\,
  Bhante Urgyen Sangharakshita. We will continue to celebrate Bhante's life
  and legacy by exploring these teachings during the centenary of his birth
 .
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/thurs-night-14-may
END:VEVENT
